# `.rx/gotchas.md` is written by every agent, appending its lesson at EOF. Two
# agents branching from the same base therefore collide there every time, on
# entries that are semantically independent and merely textually adjacent. It
# blocked 3 of 3 admin PRs at once on 5 Sep 2026 and recurred 7 more times in
# the next 24 hours; every resolution was identical — keep both blocks, order
# irrelevant. `merge=union` does exactly that, automatically. (ENG-1012)
#
# SCOPE — deliberately NOT applied to `.rx/guardrails.md` or `.rx/mockups.md`.
# Those hold rules and references that agents EDIT in place, and union is dumb:
# on an edited line it keeps BOTH versions rather than conflicting, which for a
# guardrail would mean two contradictory rules shipping unnoticed. A conflict in
# those files is the correct outcome, so they stay unmanaged.
#
# KNOWN LIMIT — this file is mostly-append, NOT purely append. Measured across
# the four repos: 39 of 172 commits touching gotchas.md (~23%) contain
# deletions, because entries get CORRECTED in place once they turn out to be
# wrong. This repo family has an entry that has been rewritten three times,
# its own headings reading "CORRECTED" and "RE-CORRECTED". If two CONCURRENT
# branches correct the SAME entry, union keeps the stale text AND the corrected
# text, adjacent, with no conflict — leaving a document that asserts both.
# Requiring concurrency makes that much rarer than 23%, but not rare enough to
# ignore. Detection is cheap: after a merge that touched this file, grep for
# adjacent duplicate `##` headings.
#
# WHERE THIS APPLIES — git reads .gitattributes from the checked-out worktree,
# so this takes effect on LOCAL merge and rebase, which is where the integrate
# loop resolves these. A bare server-side merge does NOT consult it: verified
# with `git merge-tree` in a bare clone, which still conflicts. So expect GitHub
# to keep reporting CONFLICTING on this file — that is the expected outcome, not
# a regression. Resolve by local rebase, which now needs no hand-editing.
#
# The durable fix is one file per entry (`.rx/gotchas/NNN-slug.md`), which has
# neither limitation — ENG-1012 option 1.
.rx/gotchas.md merge=union
